# Overview

This repository documents methodologies, evaluation criteria, and practical studies used to assess the linguistic quality of Brazilian Portuguese generated by Large Language Models (LLMs).

The objective is to evaluate whether AI-generated responses preserve meaning, context, fluency, tone, and linguistic naturalness expected from native Brazilian Portuguese speakers.

---

# Scope

The evaluation framework covers multiple linguistic dimensions commonly required in AI Quality, Human Feedback, and Large Language Model assessment projects.

The repository focuses on practical evaluation rather than software development.

---

# Evaluation Dimensions

## Semantic Accuracy

Assessment of meaning preservation throughout the generated response, identifying ambiguity, distortions, omissions, and lexical inconsistencies.

---

## Pragmatic Analysis

Evaluation of contextual understanding, conversational intent, discourse coherence, and communication objectives.

---

## Tone Consistency

Verification of language register according to the intended audience.

Examples include:

- Formal communication
- Informal communication
- Technical documentation
- Academic writing
- Institutional language
- Customer support

---

## Grammar Validation

Evaluation according to contemporary Brazilian Portuguese grammar rules, including agreement, punctuation, sentence structure, cohesion, and readability.

---

## Orthographic Review

Verification of spelling according to the current Brazilian Portuguese Orthographic Agreement.

---

## Technical Terminology

Assessment of terminology used in specialized domains, including:

- Artificial Intelligence
- Finance
- Healthcare
- Law
- Engineering
- Technology

---

## Regional Language

Evaluation of linguistic variation while preserving naturalness and consistency across Brazilian Portuguese.

